==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Glorious Amaterasu''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Amaterasu''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Shining Amaterasu is an offensive unit against enemies with traits. Keep her well protected behind meatshields and watch her deal [[Massive Damage|Massive Damage]] to traited enemies. She is both a good unit for newer players and later players, due to her typing and versatility.

If you have nothing better, you can use her against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies like [[THE SLOTH]] or [[Master A.]]. It isn't recommended due to her underwhelming damage, but she does make up for that slightly by the fact she outranges them. While most generalists lose use later in the game ([[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder God Zeus]], for example), as they do not perform as well as units specified for certain traits, this doesn't apply to Amaterasu, as she still shines throughout [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]], and well into later [[Uncanny Legends]], as she is one of the few [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic Cats]] who doesn't require [[Catfruit|Elder Catfruit]] or [[Talents|NP]]. This is somewhat countered by the fact she needs an Epic Catfruit seed and she does not have curse immune/resist talents, but you won't be grinding nearly as much.

==='''True Form'''===
Almighty Amaterasu gains a considerable attack boost, which is more than enough to justify this evolution, despite being a very simple upgrade. It brings her on par with some trait-specific attackers, despite the fact that she targets all traits.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Survive|Survive]]''' is not that necessary, but her DPS is enough to excuse that and make it worth the NP. If you're planning on investing into her Ultra Talents, however, this Talent is noticeably more useful.

'''[[Barrier Breaker]]''' has two main purposes: allowing her to break [[UltraBaaBaa]]'s and [[Youcan]]'s barriers or to avoid having to hit enemies with weak barriers twice. If you only care about being able to break otherwise unbreakable barriers, then it is recommended to only unlock the first level of this talent. Maxing it does result in shielded Aliens falling faster, but it isn't a good investment due to the existence of cheaper options for barrier breaking like [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]] that don't require as much investment.

'''[[Zombie Killer]]''', on the other hand, is an amazing Talent for Amaterasu, turning her into a sort of budget [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION Uber]]. It cuts the time she needs to get rid of zombies, but also removes the risk of them reviving in a nasty spot and, in some cases, allows her to have an effect in the first place, as some Zombies have infinite revives and can't be simply shut down by brute force.

Amaterasu relies heavily on her stats, so '''Defense Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' are of high priority, though boosting with Catseyes first is recommended. Amaterasu at Lv.50 with max talents has a whopping ''26,851 DPS'' vs Traited enemies, destroying them with terrifying ease.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Almighty Amaterasu's Ultra Talents are incredibly good and further improve her role as a generalist nuker.

'''[[Strengthen]]''' should be your main priority, as Amaterasu benefits immensely from the damage bonus provided when the effect is active. It brings her DPH/DPS up to ''316,800/~47,800'' against [[Fruit Treasures|Fruited Traits]] and ''237,600/~35,800'' against Relic and Aku at Lv.60. Furthermore, this Talent synergizes very well with her Survive Talent, allowing her an additional guaranteed reposition while Strengthened in the event that anything should happen to her (or if you end up overshooting the damage threshold necessary to put her into Strengthen range).

With the context of [[Talent Orbs]], this damage increase is even more valuable. One or two traits of your choosing can be given up to a ''.5x'' additive boost to the Massive Damage multiplier per Orb, upgrading its damage increase to a maximum of 5x against a single Fruited Trait, or 4x against Relic/Aku. However, with how difficult these Orbs are to obtain, these numbers should be considered a bonus for endgame players or those who consistently grind Talent Orbs.

'''[[Special Abilities#Dodge|Dodge Attack]]''' has a considerably lower priority than other Talents that improve either her damage or survivability for a lower NP cost. At 20%, this ability has too small of an activation rate to be consistently practical in application, despite the fact that it works against all traits. With the steep cost of unlocking a new ability, upgrading it, and said ability being an Ultra Talent, Dodge Attack should only be considered in the case of full investment.

Overall, Almighty Amaterasu's Ultra Talents don't provide anything overtly flashy, but are still a good Dark Catseye investment for players looking for a powerful generalist nuker. She not only benefits from being boosted to Lv.60 but also from Talent Orbs regardless of Talent investment.

==='''Orb'''===
Massive Damage or Berserker Orbs for better damage output.

